<title>HONG KONG: HK bourse suspends Shenzhen Int'l trade.</title>
<headline>HK bourse suspends Shenzhen Int'l trade.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in shares of optical products distributor Shenzhen International Holdings Ltd was suspended with effect from 11:40 a.m. (0340 GMT) on Tuesday at the direction of the stock exchange, the Hong Kong bourse said.  </p>
<p>The suspension was made pending an announcement, the exchange said but gave no further details.</p>
<p>Shenzhen International shares were up HK$0.12 or 25 percent to HK$0.60 prior to the suspension. Volume was 224.13 million shares worth HK$125.14 million.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
